{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-3397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14050879/state.json" "file_sha256" "874fe499780830018c708f2824d31e0038879f10565d701af8b059efa6657e2f"} {"question" "q-3397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})(2{e}^{2x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{2x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=2{e}^{2x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{2x}(\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})-\\int (\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3})(2{e}^{2x})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\int {e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}J \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}(\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}I) \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3}+\\frac{2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{9}-\\frac{4}{9}I \\\\ \\frac{13}{9}I & =\\frac{2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-3{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{9} \\\\ I & =\\frac{{e}^{2x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{13}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14050879/state.json" "file_sha256" "874fe499780830018c708f2824d31e0038879f10565d701af8b059efa6657e2f"} {"question" "q-3397" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14050879/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "7d51f9ac6e40cd86e174554bbafa9211337125098e606e5510a0bcb7968fe6bb"} {"question" "q-3397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14050879/state.json" "file_sha256" "874fe499780830018c708f2824d31e0038879f10565d701af8b059efa6657e2f"} {"question" "q-3397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{13}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{13}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-2{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)-3{e}^{2x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{13}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{13}+C"] ["math" "\\frac{{e}^{2x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{13}+C"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14050879/state.json" "file_sha256" "874fe499780830018c708f2824d31e0038879f10565d701af8b059efa6657e2f"} {"question" "q-3397" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{e}^{2x}(2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)-3\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))}{13}+C"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14050879/state.json" "file_sha256" "874fe499780830018c708f2824d31e0038879f10565d701af8b059efa6657e2f"} {"question" "q-12916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14050879/state.json" "file_sha256" "874fe499780830018c708f2824d31e0038879f10565d701af8b059efa6657e2f"} {"question" "q-12916" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To use integration by parts, let's suppose that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, using the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)-\\int (-\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)(-{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-J.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, we can use integration by parts to evaluate\n\n$$\nJ=\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nTo do this, let's suppose that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u={e}^{-x}\\, & ⇒\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-{e}^{-x}\\,, \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\, & ⇒\\,v=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula of integration by parts, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}J & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int u\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =uv-\\int v\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\int (\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)(-{e}^{-x})\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\int {e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+I.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this back into our equation for $I,$ we can subsequently solve for $I.$ We remember to add a constant of integration $C$ at the end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I & =-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-J \\\\ I & =-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-({e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+I) \\\\ I & =-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x-I \\\\ 2I & =-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x-{e}^{-x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\ I & =-\\frac{{e}^{-x}}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+\\operatorname{cos}⁡x)+C\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14050879/state.json" "file_sha256" "874fe499780830018c708f2824d31e0038879f10565d701af8b059efa6657e2f"} {"question" "q-12916" "field" ni